<section id="app-usage-analytics" aria-labelledby="app-usage-analytics-heading">
    <h2 id="app-usage-analytics-heading">App usage statistics with Firebase Analytics</h2>
    <p>SalaTime uses Google Analytics for Firebase to understand which app screens and features are used and to improve the app. The app sends fixed screen names and selected action names, such as sign-in, registration, sign-out and cloud synchronization. These events do not include the contents of the screens or API requests.</p>
    <p>The Firebase SDK also collects usage and technical information such as app launches, sessions, engagement, app version, operating system, device model and an app-instance identifier that distinguishes installations. Google may derive an approximate location from network information. This is pseudonymous usage information, not a promise of complete anonymity.</p>
    <p>SalaTime does not send account names, email addresses, account identifiers, passwords, precise GPS coordinates, search text, Quran verses, reciter selections or personal reading history to Analytics. Analytics is separate from the optional account and reading-progress synchronization described above. Collection of advertising identifiers and advertising personalization are disabled for this integration.</p>
    <p>You can turn these statistics off in <strong>SalaTime → Settings → Usage statistics</strong>, including when using the app without an account. Your choice is saved on the device. Turning collection off stops future Analytics events and clears the local Analytics data and app-instance identifier; it does not delete statistics already processed by Google. You can enable collection again from the same setting.</p>
    <p>Analytics events are sent directly to Google, rather than being processed by SalaTime's hosting. Google's handling of this data is described in its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a> and its <a href="https://support.google.com/firebase/answer/6318039" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Analytics data-collection documentation</a>.</p>
</section>
